payload.text:
The error `42P17` "infinite recursion detected in policy" occurs because the `Admins can view all profiles` policy queries the `profiles` table to check if the user is an admin. This check itself triggers the policy again, creating an infinite loop.

To fix this, we need to create a **Security Definer Function** in the database. This function bypasses Row Level Security (RLS) to safely check the admin status without triggering the loop.

### 1. Database Fix (Required)

Please copy and run the following SQL block in your **Supabase SQL Editor** to fix the issue immediately:

```sql
-- 1. Create a secure function to check admin status bypassing RLS
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION is_admin()
RETURNS BOOLEAN
LANGUAGE sql
SECURITY DEFINER
AS $$
  SELECT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM profiles
    WHERE id = auth.uid()
    AND is_admin = true
  );
$$;

-- 2. Drop the problematic recursive policy
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can view all profiles" ON profiles;

-- 3. Re-create the policy using the safe function
CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all profiles" ON profiles
FOR SELECT
USING (
  is_admin() = true
);

-- 4. (Optional) Update other admin policies to use the function for better performance
-- You can run these, or keep the previous ones (they work now because the profile recursion is fixed)
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can view all interviews" ON interviews;
CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all interviews" ON interviews FOR SELECT USING ( is_admin() = true );

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can view all cvs" ON cvs;
CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all cvs" ON cvs FOR SELECT USING ( is_admin() = true );

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can view all portfolios" ON portfolios;
CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all portfolios" ON portfolios FOR SELECT USING ( is_admin() = true );

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can view all letters" ON motivation_letters;
CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all letters" ON motivation_letters FOR SELECT USING ( is_admin() = true );
```

### 2. Code Updates

I will update `README.md` with this corrected SQL script and improve the error handling in `ProfileScreen.tsx` to detect this specific error and provide a helpful message instead of a generic warning.

